\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. My God, I love Thee- not because
\par I hope for heaven thereby,
\par Nor yet because who love Thee not
\par Are lost eternally.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou, O my Jesus, Thou didst me
\par Upon the Cross embrace;
\par For me didst bear the nails and spear,
\par And manifold disgrace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. And griefs and torments numberless,
\par And sweat of agony,
\par And death itself- and all for me,
\par Who was Thine enemy.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Then why, O blessed Jesus Christ,
\par Should I not love Thee well?
\par Not for the sake of winning heaven,
\par Or of escaping hell;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Not with the hope of gaining aught:
\par Not seeking a reward;
\par But as Thyself hast loved me,
\par O ever-looking Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. E'en so I love Thee, and will love,
\par And in Thy praise will sing;
\par Because Thou art my loving God
\par And my eternal King.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

